-- title:
--   Supersingular component from an affine chart has q+1 ends
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (so $A$ lies over $q$). Let $W$ be a finset of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places that are rational, affine geometric, and whose value at the chosen geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$; let $s\in W$. Assume $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$). Further data: intermediate fields $\mathbb Q\subseteq k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $k_0\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (an element $x$ of $K_b$ lies in $A_b$ iff its image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$), an element $\varpi_b\in A_b$, an $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, the assumption that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A) = \kappa[X,Y]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ is a domain, a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ that is an $A_b$-algebra and is stable under every level automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, a field $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ together with a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue field $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ restricting to $A$, with surjective residue map to $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal), with $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$, and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ of the $C_s$-action inside the Drinfeld function field, whose image consists exactly of those elements of that fixed field lying in the image of the coordinate ring; finally an $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebra isomorphism $e:FSS\to\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ with $e(R.\mathrm{residue}\,b)=\rho(b)$ for all $b\in B$. The conclusion: there is a finset $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with exactly $q+1$ elements such that a place $Q$ lies outside $N$ precisely when $R.\mathrm{residue}\,b$ belongs to the valuation subring of $Q$ for every $b\in B$, and such that $N$ is stable under the induced action: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ ($\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$), every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N$ iff $Q\in N$.
--
--   This is the count of the ends of the supersingular (Drinfeld–Deligne–Lusztig) component of the stable reduction: read through the chart $B$ and the isomorphism $e$, the places of $FSS$ at which the reduced chart fails to be regular are the $q+1$ points at infinity of the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and unchanged by passage to the $C_s$-fixed field, and they are permuted by the level automorphisms acting through `RegularProlongation.resAut`. It feeds the construction of the local stalks at the smooth points of the base in the semistable model of the full-level modular curve.
